; # flow_survey
;
; A survey chart of a drifting island field, every pixel computed by a Rays Lisp kernel on the
; GPU lane. It is the second iteration of `flow_contours` and keeps its idea: one animated height
; field, `(noise3 [x y drift])`, read per pixel for lines and once per cell of a square grid for
; glyphs that are boxes, rings and diagonals of cell-local distances, with no font and no texture.
;
; What it adds is the vocabulary of a film interface: a near-black ground, one bone ink in three
; thinner tints, and one signal ink that is on screen only while something happens.
;
; - `contours`: the coast is the brightest line and each line inland is fainter.
; - `plateau`: everything above the last contour is hatched, so a summit is a tone, not a hole.
; - `sea`: registration crosses on a coarse grid, only where the height under them is open sea.
; - `xs`, `dots`, `rings`, `squares`: one small glyph per band, darker outside and brighter
;   towards the summit. None fills its cell, so neighbours never join into a slab.
; - `echo` and `sparks`: the ping. A level climbs from under the coast to over the summit `rate`
;   times a second; `echo` draws the contours near it in the signal ink and `sparks` marks a
;   share of the cells in the band it is crossing. Between pings the chart is monochrome.
;
; A cell's glyph is chosen by a hash of the cell index, never of the height or the time, so a
; glyph only appears or leaves as a contour or the ping passes over its cell.
;
; ## The pointer
;
; - Its height moves the coast by `swing` levels: up is more land.
; - Its side zooms about the middle of the viewport, `reach` times in at the left and out at the
;   right.
; - The left button multiplies time by ten.
;
; A kernel cannot read a `(state ...)` value (`E_PACKED_STATE`), so nothing accumulates: there is
; no scrolled pan or wheel zoom, and the fast clock is `t` times ten, which jumps to another part
; of the drift when the button goes down and back when it comes up.
;
; ## Kernels
;
; Every layer is its own kernel of at most 64 registers, and the glyph kernel is near that limit.
; That is why a layer takes an ink and no separate opacity: a dimmer layer is drawn in a thinner
; tint (`chalk`, `ash`, `dust`, each `bone` times a number).
;
; The dataflow is pointer, controls -> `field`, `ping`, inks -> layers -> `result`. `speed`,
; `scale`, `cell`, `levels` and `base` are those of `flow_contours`; `summit` is how many contours
; there are from the coast up, `fade` how far inland the lines reach, `rate` the pings a second,
; `bone` and `signal` the two inks.
; Run: `dune exec sketches/flow_survey/main.exe`.

(workspace flow_survey

  ; A survey chart of a drifting island field, every pixel computed by a Lisp kernel on the GPU.
  ; The second iteration of flow_contours: the same height field, (noise3 [x y drift]) in units
  ; of a grid of square cells, read per pixel for lines and hatching and once per cell
  ; (cell = x - mod x 1, there is no floor) for glyphs.  New here: two inks instead of greys,
  ; lines that fade inland from the coast, a hatched summit, registration crosses on the open
  ; sea, and a ping, a level that climbs from the sea to the summit and lights what it passes
  ; in the signal ink.
  ; Each layer is its own kernel: all of them in one would not fit the 64 registers.
  ; The pointer drives it: its height moves the coast, its side zooms about the middle of the
  ; viewport, and the left button multiplies time by ten.  A kernel cannot read a (state ...)
  ; value (E_PACKED_STATE), so nothing here accumulates: no scrolled pan, and the fast clock is
  ; t times ten, which jumps when the button goes down or up.
  ; Dataflow: pointer, controls -> field, ping, inks -> layers -> result.
  ; A glyph in `share` of the cells whose height sits in contour band `level` (0 is the
  ; outermost: the middle of band 0 is the height field.middle).  A cell is chosen by its own
  ; hash, a noise of the cell index that never changes with time.  With a b the distances from
  ; the cell centre, the shape is
  ; |max(a, b) - radius| < stroke   and   |a - b| < diagonal
  ; so radius 0 is a box, a radius is a ring, and a small diagonal keeps only an x.
  (defmacro glyph [field level share radius stroke diagonal ink]
    `(let* [field# ~field
            ink# ~ink]
       (draw/image (image/map (fn [uv#]
                                (let* [one# 1
                                       half# 0.5
                                       part# 0.4
                                       x# (* uv#.x field#.columns)
                                       y# (* uv#.y field#.rows)
                                       in_x# (mod x# one#)
                                       in_y# (mod y# one#)
                                       cell_x# (- x# in_x#)
                                       cell_y# (- y# in_y#)
                                       height# (noise3 [(+ (* (+ cell_x# half#) field#.scale) field#.left) (+ (* (+ cell_y# half#) field#.scale) field#.top) field#.drift]
                                                       :octaves 2)
                                       off_band# (- (- (* height# field#.levels) field#.middle)
                                                    ~level)
                                       hash# (mod (* 61
                                                     (noise3 [(* cell_x# part#) (* cell_y# part#) half#]))
                                                  one#)
                                       a# (abs (- in_x# half#))
                                       b# (abs (- in_y# half#))
                                       chosen# (and (< (abs off_band#) part#)
                                                    (< hash# ~share))
                                       inside# (and (< (abs (- (max a# b#) ~radius)) ~stroke)
                                                    (< (abs (- a# b#)) ~diagonal))]
                                  [ink#.x ink#.y ink#.z (if (and chosen# inside#) one# 0)]))
                              :width field#.width
                              :height field#.height)
                   :at [0 0 0])))

  ; Contour lines about a pixel wide whatever the slope: the distance to the level is divided
  ; by a finite difference of the height over field.pixel, one pixel in field units.  The line at level `centre` is drawn in
  ; full and the ones around it fade to nothing `reach` levels away, so centre 0 is a
  ; bright coast with fainter lines inland, and a moving centre is a ping.
  (defmacro lines [field centre reach ink]
    `(let* [field# ~field
            ink# ~ink]
       (draw/image (image/map (fn [uv#]
                                (let* [one# 1
                                       half# 0.5
                                       x# (+ (* (* uv#.x field#.columns) field#.scale)
                                             field#.left)
                                       y# (+ (* (* uv#.y field#.rows) field#.scale)
                                             field#.top)
                                       height# (noise3 [x# y# field#.drift] :octaves 2)
                                       slope_x# (- (noise3 [(+ x# field#.pixel) y# field#.drift]
                                                           :octaves 2)
                                                   height#)
                                       slope_y# (- (noise3 [x# (+ y# field#.pixel) field#.drift]
                                                           :octaves 2)
                                                   height#)
                                       band# (- (* height# field#.levels) field#.base)
                                       to_level# (abs (- (mod (+ band# half#) one#) half#))
                                       pixels# (/ to_level#
                                                  (* field#.levels
                                                     (sqrt (+ (* slope_x# slope_x#)
                                                              (* slope_y# slope_y#)))))
                                       near# (- one# (/ (abs (- band# ~centre)) ~reach))]
                                  [ink#.x ink#.y ink#.z (if (> band# (- 0 half#)) (* (max 0 near#) (max 0 (- one# (* pixels# 0.8)))) 0)]))
                              :width field#.width
                              :height field#.height)
                   :at [0 0 0])))

  ; Diagonal hatching over everything above contour `level`: a stripe every `spacing` pixels,
  ; inked within `thin` of its middle (0.5 is solid).  The middle, not the edge, so a pixel
  ; whose stripe phase is a round number never falls on the comparison.
  (defmacro hatch [field level spacing thin ink]
    `(let* [field# ~field
            ink# ~ink]
       (draw/image (image/map (fn [uv#]
                                (let* [x# (* uv#.x field#.columns)
                                       y# (* uv#.y field#.rows)
                                       height# (noise3 [(+ (* x# field#.scale) field#.left) (+ (* y# field#.scale) field#.top) field#.drift]
                                                       :octaves 2)
                                       band# (- (* height# field#.levels) field#.base)
                                       stripe# (mod (/ (+ (* uv#.x field#.width)
                                                          (* uv#.y field#.height))
                                                       ~spacing)
                                                    1)]
                                  [ink#.x ink#.y ink#.z (if (and (> band# ~level) (< (abs (- stripe# 0.5)) ~thin)) 1 0)]))
                              :width field#.width
                              :height field#.height)
                   :at [0 0 0])))

  ; Registration crosses on the open sea: one every `every` cells, with arms `arm` cells long
  ; and `thin` cells thick, kept only where the height under its centre is below the coast.
  (defmacro crosses [field every arm thin ink]
    `(let* [field# ~field
            ink# ~ink]
       (draw/image (image/map (fn [uv#]
                                (let* [every# ~every
                                       middle# (/ every# 2)
                                       x# (* uv#.x field#.columns)
                                       y# (* uv#.y field#.rows)
                                       in_x# (mod x# every#)
                                       in_y# (mod y# every#)
                                       height# (noise3 [(+ (* (+ (- x# in_x#) middle#) field#.scale) field#.left) (+ (* (+ (- y# in_y#) middle#) field#.scale) field#.top) field#.drift]
                                                       :octaves 2)
                                       band# (- (* height# field#.levels) field#.base)
                                       a# (abs (- in_x# middle#))
                                       b# (abs (- in_y# middle#))]
                                  [ink#.x ink#.y ink#.z (if (and (< band# -1) (and (< (min a# b#) ~thin) (< (max a# b#) ~arm))) 1 0)]))
                              :width field#.width
                              :height field#.height)
                   :at [0 0 0])))

  (graph picture :context draw
    (let* [
           ; how fast the field drifts
           speed 0.02
           ; blob size: smaller is bigger
           scale 0.05
           ; side of a glyph cell, in pixels
           cell 10.0
           ; contour density
           levels 48.0
           ; height of the coast, the outermost contour, with the pointer mid-window
           base 24.0
           ; how far the pointer's height moves the coast: up is more land
           swing 4.0
           ; how far the pointer's side zooms: this many times in at the left, out at the right
           reach 2.5
           ; the pointer in the window, 0..1 from the left and from the top
           across (/ (max 0 (min (frame/width) (pointer/x))) (max 1 (frame/width)))
           down (/ (max 0 (min (frame/height) (pointer/y))) (max 1 (frame/height)))
           ; time, ten times faster while the left button is down
           clock (* t (if (pointer/down) 10 1))
           ; contours from the coast to the summit
           summit 5.0
           ; the contour lines fade to nothing this many levels inland of the coast
           fade (+ summit 1)
           ; pings a second
           rate 0.15
           ; the ink of the chart
           bone [0.91 0.89 0.84]
           ; the ink of the ping
           signal [1.0 0.3 0.05]
           ; the chart ink, thinned three times: every layer is drawn in one of these
           chalk (* bone 0.85)
           ash (* bone 0.6)
           dust (* bone 0.3)
           ; the one height field every layer reads, and the picture it is drawn on: the
           ; whole viewport, cut into square cells
           zoomed (* scale (pow reach (- (* across 2) 1)))
           coast (+ base (* swing (- (* down 2) 1)))
           field {:width (frame/width)
                  :height (frame/height)
                  :columns (/ (frame/width) cell)
                  :rows (/ (frame/height) cell)
                  :left (* (/ zoomed cell) (/ (frame/width) -2))
                  :top (* (/ zoomed cell) (/ (frame/height) -2))
                  :drift (* clock speed)
                  :scale zoomed
                  :levels levels
                  :base coast
                  :middle (+ coast 0.5)
                  :pixel (/ zoomed cell)}
           ; the level the ping is at: it starts under the coast and leaves over the summit
           ping (* (- (mod (* clock rate) 1) 0.2) (+ summit 2))
           background (draw/background "#0b0c0e")
           sea (crosses field 8 0.7 0.08 dust)
           plateau (hatch field summit 6.0 0.1 ash)
           contours (lines field 0 fade chalk)
           xs (glyph field 0 0.7 0 0.26 0.07 ash)
           dots (glyph field 1 0.7 0 0.07 1 chalk)
           rings (glyph field 2 0.5 0.26 0.06 1 chalk)
           squares (glyph field 3 0.6 0 0.2 1 bone)
           echo (lines field ping 1.5 signal)
           sparks (glyph field ping 0.2 0 0.3 1 signal)]
      (draw/merge background sea plateau contours xs dots rings squares echo sparks)))

  (graph settings :context settings
    (settings/config :title "Survey: contours in glyphs, with a ping"
                     :width 1500
                     :height 900))

  (graph editor :context editor
    (let* [preview (ui/canvas (ref picture))
           network (ui/graph "picture" :focus true)
           inspector (ui/inspector :of network)
           outline (ui/outline)
           network_dock (ui/split-at "horizontal" 0.5 outline network)
           split_at (ui/split "horizontal"
                              preview
                              (ui/split "horizontal"
                                        network_dock
                                        inspector
                                        :second_size 260)
                              :second_size 880)]
      (ui/workspace split_at))))

(layout (panel ["editor" "network"] :collapsed false)
        (panel ["editor" "outline"] :collapsed true)
        (node ["picture" "clock#1#else"] :at [-48 216] :collapsed true)
        (node ["picture" "clock#1#then"] :at [-48 120] :collapsed true)
        (node ["picture" "contours"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "dots"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "echo"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "plateau"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "rings"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "sea"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "sparks"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "squares"] :level "chip")
        (node ["picture" "xs"] :level "chip"))
